---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Nepali Data Studio | DoAI × ILPRL Project"
  description="A provenance-first open data platform for Nepali and Nepal-based languages: sourcing, curation, annotation, and release for LLM development."
  activeTab="projects"
>
  <div class="detail-header">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span> <a href="/projects">Projects</a> <span>/</span> <span>Nepali Data Studio</span>
      </div>
      <div class="project-badges" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-active">Active Project</span>
        <span class="badge badge-category">Corpus Engineering & Platform</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="detail-title">Nepali Data Studio (नेपाली डाटा स्टुडियो)</h1>
      <p class="detail-subtitle">
        A Provenance-First Open Data Platform for Nepali & Nepal-Based Languages: Sourcing, Curation, Annotation, Instruction Data, and Release for LLM Development.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="container">
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="detail-main">
        <div class="detail-section">
          <h2>1. Executive Summary & Problem Context</h2>
          <p>
            Nepali is spoken by tens of millions of people worldwide but remains severely low-resource in the modern LLM era (reporting only ~4.18B public tokens, over 80× fewer than English). Existing Devanagari text in large multilingual web scrapes (such as FineWeb-2, Sangraha, and IndicCorp) suffers from <strong>silent Hindi leakage, broken legacy fonts (Preeti/Kantipur), high duplication rates, and severed provenance</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once scraped text is merged into a flat file, its original publisher, license, crawl date, and annotator identity disappear. <strong>Nepali Data Studio (NDS)</strong> is an all-in-one data operating system built on <strong>Datasette and SQLite</strong> that tracks the full life of Nepali data with 100% auditable lineage.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <strong>Core Principle:</strong> Every single training example retains parentage from source to raw file, document, sentence, annotation, and instruction release.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-section">
          <h2>2. The 6-Database Architecture</h2>
          <p>
            NDS avoids fragile infrastructure by running on SQLite with Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) and Litestream replication. Data is partitioned into six purpose-built databases:
          </p>
          <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
            <li><strong><code>registry.db</code>:</strong> Sources, licenses, crawl policies, and external dataset aliases (linking past KU research papers and Hugging Face benchmarks).</li>
            <li><strong><code>raw.db</code>:</strong> Untouchable vault of immutable, SHA-256 hashed HTML, PDF, image, and audio files.</li>
            <li><strong><code>corpus.db</code>:</strong> Normalized (NFC, Preeti-converted) text, Devanagari sentences, tokens (MPP 43 & UPOS), and gazetteers.</li>
            <li><strong><code>annotation.db</code>:</strong> Standoff annotation workbench, multi-rater votes, and gold adjudications.</li>
            <li><strong><code>instruct.db</code>:</strong> Prompt templates, instruction-response pairs, and DPO/RLHF preference pairs.</li>
            <li><strong><code>release.db</code> & <code>admin.db</code>:</strong> Release snapshots, Croissant-RAI metadata, contributor credit ledgers, and audit logs.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-section">
          <h2>3. Annotation Hub & Plugin Manifests</h2>
          <p>
            Instead of building custom software for every task, NDS tasks are specified as <strong>declarative YAML manifests + JSON Schemas</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Core P0 Tasks:</strong> 10-class Named Entity Recognition (NER), Part-of-Speech tagging (MPP 43 tagset), Spelling & Grammar Error Correction (GEC), Question Answering (QA), and Gemma/T5 chat instruction pairs.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <strong>Perspectivism:</strong> Multi-annotator disagreements are never discarded. They are preserved for linguistic analysis, and AI suggestions are strictly marked as <code>origin = machine</code> and never auto-promoted to Gold.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sidebar -->
      <aside class="detail-sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-box">
          <h3>Project Metadata</h3>
          <ul class="sidebar-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Candidate / Student</strong>
              Sundeep Dawadi (Dept. of AI, KU)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Academic Supervisor</strong>
              Mr. Sunil Regmi (Lecturer & Coordinator, DoAI)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mentor & Domain Lead</strong>
              Prof. Dr. Bal Krishna Bal (Dean, SoE & Lead, ILPRL)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Duration & Phase</strong>
              12 Weeks (Phase 1 Platform Deliverable)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Core Technology</strong>
              Datasette (1.0 alpha series), SQLite (WAL), Litestream
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Open Deliverable</strong>
              GitHub: <code>ILPRL/NepaliDataStudio</code>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="sidebar-box">
          <h3>Resources & Links</h3>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <a
              href="https://github.com/ILPRL/NepaliDataStudio"
              class="btn btn-primary"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              style="justify-content: center;"
            >
              GitHub Repository ↗
            </a>
            <a
              href="/projects"
              class="btn btn-secondary"
              style="justify-content: center;"
            >
              ← Back to All Projects
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
